  "id": "Compound::DB01184 - Gene::1551",
  "verbalization": "Domperidone is likely to influence Cyp3a7 through a shared pathway involving Aromatase Activity. The evidence suggests that Domperidone binds to Cyp3a5, Cyp2c8, and Cyp2d6, all of which participate in Aromatase Activity, which in turn is participated by Cyp3a7. This indicates that Domperidone may inhibit Cyp3a7 by targeting one of its substrates, thereby reducing Aromatase Activity. The final scores from the paths support a direct mechanistic link, with the highest confidence in the interaction between Domperidone and Cyp3a7 through the Aromatase Activity pathway. The consistent involvement of Cyp3a7 in Aromatase Activity across the three paths strengthens the hypothesis that Domperidone exerts its effect on Cyp3a7 via this route. The mechanism is supported by the presence of a binding interaction between Domperidone and multiple cytochrome P450 enzymes, which are known to be involved in drug metabolism and enzyme induction.",
